<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#hoplite">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hoplite</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A hoplite was a heavily armed Greek infantryman, equipped with a large round shield, spear and armour, fighting in the close formation known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/phalanx">phalanx</a>. Hoplite armies proved effective against the lighter-armed Persian infantry. They were the backbone of Greek resistance to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-persian-wars">Greco-Persian Wars</a>.</p></div>
